From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 08 Oct 2026 09:40:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: re-arm the beacon monitor after it reports a loss

The driver monitors beacons for a station link itself. At each
periodic check, it compares the time of the last beacon with the loss
limit. A report does not restart the limit. While beacons stay absent,
every check after the limit reports the loss again. mac80211 sends a
connection quality event for each report. It also starts a new probe
when no earlier probe is in progress.

Restart the limit when a link reports a loss; each link of a
multi-link station keeps its own limit. A link without beacons then
reports once per limit, close to the rate of the mac80211 beacon
timer. While a scan runs on any band, the check neither reports nor
restarts the limit. mac80211 drops a report during a scan and runs no
connection timer for this driver. The first check after an on-channel
scan or a scan of another band thus reports at once if the limit
passed. A dead AP still fails a later probe and causes a disconnect.

Fixes: d915a31bbd21 ("wifi: mt76: add per-link beacon monitoring for MLO")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mac80211.c |   29 ++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -2391,20 +2391,31 @@ static void mt76_beacon_mon_iter(void *d
 		if (mt76_vif_link_phy(mlink) != phy)
 			continue;
 
-		if (time_after(jiffies,
-			       READ_ONCE(mlink->beacon_mon_last) +
-			       MT76_BEACON_MON_MAX_MISS * mlink->beacon_mon_interval))
-			ieee80211_beacon_loss(vif);
+		if (!time_after(jiffies,
+				READ_ONCE(mlink->beacon_mon_last) +
+				MT76_BEACON_MON_MAX_MISS * mlink->beacon_mon_interval))
+			continue;
+
+		WRITE_ONCE(mlink->beacon_mon_last, jiffies);
+		ieee80211_beacon_loss(vif);
 	}
 }
 
 void mt76_beacon_mon_check(struct mt76_phy *phy)
 {
-	if (phy->offchannel)
-		return;
+	struct mt76_dev *dev = phy->dev;
 
-	ieee80211_iterate_active_interfaces_atomic(phy->hw,
-		IEEE80211_IFACE_ITER_RESUME_ALL,
-		mt76_beacon_mon_iter, phy);
+	/* mac80211 drops a beacon loss report while it scans and does not
+	 * repeat it for this driver, so the check waits and keeps the
+	 * limit. The mutex orders the check after a scan completion, which
+	 * queues the mac80211 work that ends the scan before the work that
+	 * takes the report.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&dev->mutex);
+	if (!phy->offchannel && !dev->scan.req)
+		ieee80211_iterate_active_interfaces_atomic(phy->hw,
+			IEEE80211_IFACE_ITER_RESUME_ALL,
+			mt76_beacon_mon_iter, phy);
+	mutex_unlock(&dev->mutex);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mt76_beacon_mon_check);
